1
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:16,037
A Type 54, Blackstar.

2
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,877
It's the gun. Why?

3
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:18,937
Why here?

4
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,020
Why does he have that gun?

5
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:02,930
Yeah,

6
00:01:03,013 --> 00:01:07,477
yeah,

7
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:12,080
yeah.

8
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:31,500
What it means to be strong, to be brave.

9
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:40,600
I thought somehow I could
learn those things from Kirito.

10
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,800
I don't want to die.

11
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:20,580
A grenade!

12
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,920
I'm slowing you down.

13
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,200
Just leave me.

14
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,620
Not the horse.

15
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:15,160
It can go fast, but
it's too hard to handle.

16
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:36,840
Xenon, get your rifle, and blow
that horse away. Huh? What?

17
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:40,380
Alright, I'll try.

18
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:54,560
No, my finger.

19
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:00,040
I can't pull it.

20
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,040
I can't do it.

21
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,140
I can't pull the trigger.

22
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,460
Hang on tight.

23
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,720
It's no use.

24
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:32,620
We can still get away.

25
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,020
Stay sharp, damn it!

26
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:46,670
No!

27
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,500
He's catching up!

28
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,420
Hurry, faster!

29
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,200
Please, don't let him catch up to us!

30
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,920
Help me.

31
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,197
I can't do this.

32
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,480
I don't want to die!

33
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:35,420
Hey, Xenon!

34
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,482
Snap out of it!

35
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:39,581
Listen, he's catching up with us.

36
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:41,840
Pick up your gun and shoot him!

37
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:43,820
No, I can't!

38
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,237
You don't have to hit him.

39
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,400
Just distract him!

40
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:48,640
I can't!

41
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:50,180
Don't make me!

42
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:51,340
Don't make me!

43
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:53,257
Then get up here and steer this thing.

44
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:55,516
Give me your gun, and I'll shoot him.

45
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:57,610
Hecate.

46
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,940
She's part of me.

47
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:02,341
I'm the only one who can use her.

48
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,340
I can't do it.

49
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,057
I can't shoot.

50
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:20,493
I can't move my finger.

51
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:21,777
I can't.

52
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:25,040
I can't fight anymore. You can.

53
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,999
Everyone can fight if they want to.

54
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:29,957
It's your choice, so what'll it be?

55
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:32,099
Will you give up or will you fight?

56
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:37,240
If it's my choice, then I
don't want to fight anymore.

57
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:38,890
I'm done.

58
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,084
I don't want to suffer anymore.

59
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:44,942
I thought I could get
stronger playing this game.

60
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,840
But I was wrong.

61
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:52,000
I'll help you, But you have to try.

62
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,260
So come on.

63
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:54,580
You can do this.

64
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,280
It's no good.

65
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:03,220
With all this shaking around,
I can't lock on. It's okay.

66
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:07,760
The shaking's gonna stop in 3, 2, 1, now!

67
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:13,297
How's he do it?

68
00:08:13,380 --> 00:08:15,200
How can he be so calm now?

69
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:19,040
No, it's not that he's being calm.

70
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,720
He's giving it everything he's got.

71
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:26,840
When he fights, he goes all
out every time. No excuses.

72
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,460
That's it.

73
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:31,660
That's where he gets his strength.

74
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,860
I missed.

75
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:47,260
Let's go.

76
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:23,860
This isn't good.

77
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:25,957
We're like sitting ducks out here.

78
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,628
We need to find some cover.

79
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,480
Hey, I think I see a cave over there.

80
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:39,060
If we hide inside, we
can avoid the SAT scan.

81
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,040
Sounds good. Let's go.

82
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,460
This is perfect.

83
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:57,015
We can dodge the scan and rest up too.

84
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,991
What happened back there?

85
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:14,709
It's like he just popped
up out of nowhere.

86
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,965
We didn't see him on the scan.

87
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:20,219
That must mean he's got
some kind of cloaking skill.

88
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,242
Is there a skill like that here?

89
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:23,630
Invisibility?

90
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:25,520
Yeah, there is.

91
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:29,280
It's a skill called
metamaterial optical camouflage.

92
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:33,960
We're safe.

93
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,081
For now, anyway.

94
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,697
Even if he's invisible,
the sands are rough here.

95
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:40,817
We'll hear it crunching under his boots.

96
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,137
We'll see his footprints, too, so...

97
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:45,396
He can't sneak up like he did before.

98
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:47,290
Roger that.

99
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:50,404
Well, I guess we'll keep
our eyes and ears open.

100
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,840
Hey, Kirito.

101
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:02,837
Do you think there's a chance Death
Gun was killed in that explosion?

102
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:03,750
No.

103
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:08,720
The second before that truck blew up,
I saw him jump off of that robot horse.

104
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:14,000
He might have gotten dinged up, but I
can't believe that blast killed him.

105
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,190
Oh.

106
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:22,277
When he had me in his sights back at
the stadium, I thought I was a goner.

107
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,837
How'd you know I was in trouble?

108
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:26,920
And how'd you get to me so
fast from your position?

109
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,940
We were wrong about
Jushi X being Death Gun.

110
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:33,460
I took one look and I knew it wasn't.

111
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:35,562
It was pretty obvious, actually.

112
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:36,790
Obvious?

113
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:39,140
Yeah, I know a woman when I see one.

114
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,530
Oh.

115
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:43,938
The second I saw her, I knew
we overlooked something.

116
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,708
I didn't know what, though.

117
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:51,440
Oh, by the way, even though our handle
says Jushi, she calls herself Musketeer X.

118
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:53,810
Anyway,

119
00:11:53,893 --> 00:11:55,680
after I took out Musketeer X,

120
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:59,664
I looked over to the south and
saw you lying there in the street.

121
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:05,177
I knew you were in trouble, so I grabbed
her rifle and grenades and charged in,

122
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:07,966
shooting and tossing
bombs as fast as I could.

123
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:17,006
I can't believe I let
my guard down like that.

124
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,276
Don't go beating yourself up over it.

125
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:27,197
I mean, look, it's not like I knew
he was hiding down there either.

126
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:30,120
And if our roles were
flipped, you know what?

127
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:33,045
I would have been the
one getting shot instead.

128
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:38,331
But that's okay, because I know you
would have rescued me too, wouldn't you?

129
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,157
I can't believe it.

130
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,800
My rival's trying to make me feel better.

131
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:49,117
He knows I'm weak, and
here he is, consoling me.

132
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,100
Like I'm a kid or something.

133
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,357
I'm heading out for a bit.

134
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:58,397
You might as well kick back
here and rest up while you can.

135
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,157
I wish you could log out,
but I know you can't.

136
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:03,299
Not till the tourney's over anyway.

137
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,917
You're going after Death Gun, aren't you?

138
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,118
You think you can take him on alone?

139
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,317
Yeah, I have to.

140
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:20,635
He's tough and he won't go down without
getting off a shot or two at me.

141
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:24,299
If it comes down to that,
I don't know what I'll do.

142
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,400
I might bail.

143
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:31,086
I don't want to leave you hanging like
that, so it's better if I face him alone.

144
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,060
Then you're scared of him too?

145
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,100
Yeah, I am.

146
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:40,502
If it was the old me, I would have
jumped right in and fought him.

147
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:42,997
Even if there was a
chance I was going to die.

148
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:44,060
But not anymore.

149
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:47,367
These days, there's
things I have to protect.

150
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,000
I can't die.

151
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,257
I don't want to.

152
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,100
Things you have to protect?

153
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:57,240
Yeah, in the virtual world,
and the real one, too.

154
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:02,551
Okay, then don't go after him,
just stay here and keep low.

155
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,077
As long as B .O .B.

156
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,000
is going on, we can't log out.

157
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:09,717
But once the competition's whittled
down to us and one other player,

158
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:12,447
we can suicide out and
let the other guy win.

159
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,388
That'll end the tournament.

160
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:15,918
Yeah, I don't know.

161
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,097
I mean, that's one way of doing it.

162
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:21,160
Thing is, it's not really a good option.

163
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:24,357
If we just sit here and
wait for the tourney to end,

164
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:28,205
there's no telling how many other
players that guy's gonna kill.

165
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:30,110
Yeah.

166
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:35,120
You really are strong, after all.

167
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,120
I'm not gonna hide, either.

168
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:42,870
Huh?

169
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:46,620
I'm going outside and help
you take that bastard out.

170
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:47,860
No, you're not.

171
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,177
Haven't you been listening?

172
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:51,417
If he shoots you, there's
a chance you'll die.

173
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,000
As a player, close combat's my specialty.

174
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:55,162
It's not yours.

175
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:59,297
You're in way more danger than me,
cause he can be invisible if he wants.

176
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:01,380
He'll pop up next to you and bang.

177
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,780
I don't care if I die.

178
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,564
I was scared out of my
mind back at the stadium.

179
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,580
I was scared I was gonna die.

180
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:16,080
I was even weaker than I was five years
ago, like a screaming, crying little girl.

181
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:22,040
If that's how I'm going to be for the
rest of my life, I'd rather be dead.

182
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:24,920
It's only natural to be afraid.

183
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:27,917
I don't know anyone who's
not afraid of dying.

184
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,920
Yeah, well, I hate it.

185
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,000
I'm tired of being afraid.

186
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,900
I'm so tired.

187
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:36,470
Whatever.

188
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,380
I'm not asking to go with you.

189
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,920
I'll fight by myself.

190
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,580
You want to fight alone and die alone?

191
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,668
Is that what you're saying?

192
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:48,690
Yeah.

193
00:15:48,773 --> 00:15:50,860
I was always supposed to die alone.

194
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:53,720
Let go.

195
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:55,540
I have to do this.

196
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,000
You got it all wrong.

197
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:59,640
There's no dying alone.

198
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:01,175
It's not that simple.

199
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:06,217
When you die, you leave a hole in all
the people whose lives you were part of.

200
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:08,888
And like it or not,
you're part of mine now.

201
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:11,707
Yeah, well, I never
asked to be a part of it.

202
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:15,420
Besides, my life's no one
else's business but mine.

203
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:16,910
You're wrong.

204
00:16:16,993 --> 00:16:19,332
We're involved in each other's lives now.

205
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,320
All right.

206
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:26,739
If that's how it is, then you can
protect me for the rest of my life!

207
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:35,320
You don't know anything!

208
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:39,440
And you can't do anything, so
don't go saying stuff like that!

209
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:44,720
This isn't your fight! It's
mine! Mine! You got that?

210
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,030
What?

211
00:16:47,113 --> 00:16:51,520
Even if I lose, even if I die, no
one can blame me for what I did.

212
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:54,940
You wanna help?

213
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,137
You gonna carry this burden with me?

214
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,560
Then what, huh?

215
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:04,897
You gonna hold my hands?

216
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:07,568
Even though they've got
blood all over them?

217
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,360
You murderer!

218
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,080
You kill anyone today!

219
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:22,510
Ew!

220
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:23,880
Don't touch me!

221
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:25,394
You get me all bloody!

222
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:27,368
Why don't you see yourself?

223
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:29,017
Murderer! Sorry!

224
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:35,940
I don't know.

225
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:01,680
I hate your guts! I hate you!

226
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:23,100
Even though I hate your guts...

227
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,120
Can I borrow your lap for a sec?

228
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:36,170
I...

229
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,960
I killed someone.

230
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:48,400
About five years ago, in a small town up
north, this guy tried to rob a post office.

231
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:54,000
The news said the robber died because
his gun went off accidentally.

232
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:57,940
But the truth is, I was there.

233
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,780
I grabbed his gun and shot him dead.

234
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,940
How old were you?

235
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:05,660
Eleven years old.

236
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:11,300
And ever since then, whenever I see a gun,
I start throwing up and then I pass out.

237
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:13,460
If I see a gun,

238
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:18,120
I see the face of the robber, the
way he looked right before he died.

239
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:23,980
And then I get so scared. Really? Yeah.

240
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:27,260
But in this world, I
don't have those problems.

241
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:30,060
And that got me thinking,

242
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:33,640
if I can become the
strongest player in the game,

243
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:38,520
then I'll be strong IRL too, and
maybe even forget what I did,

244
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,920
but just now, I mean,

245
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:45,480
when Death Gun had me
pinned, I was terrified,

246
00:19:45,940 --> 00:19:49,080
and just like that, I
wasn't seen on anymore,

247
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:51,280
I was the real me again.

248
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:55,700
I'm scared to die. I am.

249
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,240
Although, what's worse is,

250
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:02,000
living with this fear, it's
so painful I'd rather be dead.

251
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:09,340
But I know, if I run away from Death Gun
in my past, I'll end up weaker than before.

252
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:10,920
I will.

253
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:12,040
I know it.

254
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:15,370
Yeah.

255
00:20:15,453 --> 00:20:16,283
I get it.

256
00:20:16,366 --> 00:20:19,240
I killed someone once, too. What?

257
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:24,020
I mentioned it once, about
how I knew Death Gun.

258
00:20:24,580 --> 00:20:27,639
We fought before when we
were stuck in another game.

259
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:30,040
I'm sure you heard of it.

260
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:32,860
Sword Art Online.

261
